// Out-of-process connector plugin transport (ADR-010).
//
// A third-party connector runs as its own gRPC server implementing
// ConnectorPlugin; the hub dials it and adapts it to the in-process
// sdk.Connector interface. The connector receives ONLY its own per-call
// credential (Config.token) — never the hub's token vault or any other
// tenant's data.
//
// Emit and Checkpoint are hub-side callbacks, so the sync RPCs are
// server-streaming: the plugin streams a sequence of SyncEvents (each an
// emitted Document, an intermediate checkpoint cursor, or the terminal Done
// carrying the final cursor). The hub processes events as they arrive; if a
// hub-side Emit/Checkpoint fails the hub cancels the stream, which surfaces to
// the plugin as a context error from Send — preserving the in-process
